{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2tqylfp6js5ou5yawdccnrwm4h2feqzzgyvgdhel2pvfsw6zyfia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration (definition of done)\n\nThe C library is small: `CMakeLists.txt` globs `src/lib.c` into one shared lib. I built it with cmake and ran `nm -D --defined-only` on the resulting `.so`:\n\n```\nC  .so exports:  hex2bin\nRust .so exports: hex2bin\ndiff (C \\ Rust):  <empty>\n```\n\nThe public header (`include/lib.h`) declares exactly one function and contains **no namespace-renaming macros**, so the final linker symbol is plain `hex2bin`. Full ABI surface = 1 symbol, fully covered.\n\n## Translation notes (`translation/src/lib.rs`)\n\nThe C code is libsodium-style branch-free hex decoding, which relies heavily on C integer promotion + truncation. I reproduced that exactly rather than \"cleaning it up\":\n\n- `c_num0`/`c_alpha0` masks are computed in wrapping `u32` (matching C's promotion to `unsigned int` because of the `10U`/`55U` literals) and then truncated back to `u8` — this is what makes `(c_num - 10U) >> 8` yield `0xFF`, not `0x00FFFFFF`.\n- `state = ~state` toggles `0 → 0xFF → 0` via `u8` truncation; `c_val * 16U` uses `wrapping_mul`.\n- **Preserved quirk:** C's `strchr(ignore, c)` treats the terminating NUL as part of the ignore string, so an embedded NUL byte in `hex` is silently *skipped* whenever `ignore != NULL` and `state == 0`. My `strchr_found` helper checks `b == c` **before** `b == 0`, replicating this. A \"correct\" implementation would diverge here.\n- Preserved the exact check order (`bin_maxlen` overflow check happens *after* nibble decode), the `hex_pos--` on odd-nibble termination (via `wrapping_sub`), `bin_pos = 0` on error, and the `hex_end_p`-NULL-implies-must-consume-all-input rule.\n\n## Verification beyond compiling\n\nI wrote a `dlopen`-based differential harness comparing the C `.so` and Rust `.so` on return value, the **entire** output buffer (pre-filled with `0xAA` to catch stray writes), and the `hex_end_p` offset:\n\n- 4M randomized cases: valid hex, mixed separators, embedded NULs, fully random bytes; 9 different ignore sets (incl. `NULL`, `\"\"`, sets containing hex digits); varying `bin_maxlen`; both `hex_end_p` modes.\n- Exhaustive sweep of all 65,536 two-byte inputs × 9 ignore sets × 3 `bin_maxlen` values × 2 end-pointer modes.\n- Edge cases: `NULL` bin, zero length, `NULL` hex.\n\n**Result: `cases=7538946 fails=0`** — byte-identical output. Scratch artifacts (cmake build dir, harness) were removed; `c_src/` is unmodified (original timestamps intact). `cargo build --release` succeeds with no warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":30402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":338,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6525ad84-ab96-4172-9fdd-5ba11d1a56f2","uuid":"8a6b7d0a-6f24-4003-88dc-cf43ec7e244f","timestamp":"2026-08-26T22:03:00.572Z"}
